<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fundŭlus</span></b> , i, m.
		dim.
		fundus. * <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of sausage</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">FUNDULUM a fundo, quod non ut reliquae partes,
					sed ex una parte sola apertum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 111</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In mechanics, <i>a kind of sucker</i> or
				<i>piston</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambulatiles,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr.
					10, 13</span></i>
			.</div>
